From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:34:23 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: v4l2-mem2mem: support detached buffers for pipelined
 dispatch

Plain job_finish() warns for every HOLD_CAPTURE-capable queue, even when
the current source is a final slice. buf_done_and_job_finish() releases
OUTPUT and final CAPTURE immediately, so neither API can hand both active
buffers to an asynchronous frame slot while releasing the scheduler.

Add job_finish_detach() to atomically remove the current pair and finish
dispatch without completing either buffer. Document the driver's DMA
ownership and eventual completion obligations. Reject partial HOLD slices;
they continue to use the existing held-buffer completion API.

Use this handoff for AVD's final slices to preserve early dispatch and
VP/PP overlap. Return slot-owned buffers only after tagged retirement or
quiesced recovery. Reject stale deferred submit work whose context no
longer owns the running m2m dispatch. Keep existing HOLD warnings intact.

Exercise the production core helpers and AVD submit/send/retire with a
strict host scheduler: held/final slices, overlapping pictures, two
contexts, capacity and inbox retries, stale work and error paths.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>

[j604: backport, v4l2-mem2mem.c and v4l2-mem2mem.h hunks only. The AVD hunks of this commit
 (avd-queue.c/.h, avd-protocol.rst, tests/) arrive with the AVD driver sync that follows.]

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
(cherry picked from commit 6e3a36cd298ed36d9962641849a7596181b9171f)
---
 drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/media/v4l2-mem2mem.h           | 18 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 46 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c
index a65cbb124c..d8122b509d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-mem2mem.c
@@ -503,6 +503,34 @@ void v4l2_m2m_job_finish(struct v4l2_m2m_dev *m2m_dev,
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(v4l2_m2m_job_finish);
 
+void v4l2_m2m_job_finish_detach(struct v4l2_m2m_dev *m2m_dev,
+			      struct v4l2_m2m_ctx *m2m_ctx)
+{
+	struct vb2_v4l2_buffer *src_buf, *dst_buf;
+	bool schedule_next = false;
+	unsigned long flags;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&m2m_dev->job_spinlock, flags);
+	if (WARN_ON(m2m_dev->curr_ctx != m2m_ctx))
+		goto unlock;
+	src_buf = v4l2_m2m_next_src_buf(m2m_ctx);
+	dst_buf = v4l2_m2m_next_dst_buf(m2m_ctx);
+	/* Partial slices must use buf_done_and_job_finish() and keep CAPTURE. */
+	if (WARN_ON(!src_buf || !dst_buf ||
+		    (src_buf->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_M2M_HOLD_CAPTURE_BUF)))
+		goto unlock;
+
+	v4l2_m2m_src_buf_remove(m2m_ctx);
+	v4l2_m2m_dst_buf_remove(m2m_ctx);
+	dst_buf->is_held = false;
+	schedule_next = _v4l2_m2m_job_finish(m2m_dev, m2m_ctx);
+ unlock:
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&m2m_dev->job_spinlock, flags);
+	if (schedule_next)
+		v4l2_m2m_schedule_next_job(m2m_dev, m2m_ctx);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(v4l2_m2m_job_finish_detach);
+
 void v4l2_m2m_buf_done_and_job_finish(struct v4l2_m2m_dev *m2m_dev,
 				      struct v4l2_m2m_ctx *m2m_ctx,
 				      enum vb2_buffer_state state)
diff --git a/include/media/v4l2-mem2mem.h b/include/media/v4l2-mem2mem.h
index 31de25d792..5284bc506f 100644
--- a/include/media/v4l2-mem2mem.h
+++ b/include/media/v4l2-mem2mem.h
@@ -200,6 +200,24 @@ void v4l2_m2m_try_schedule(struct v4l2_m2m_ctx *m2m_ctx);
 void v4l2_m2m_job_finish(struct v4l2_m2m_dev *m2m_dev,
 			 struct v4l2_m2m_ctx *m2m_ctx);
 
+/**
+ * v4l2_m2m_job_finish_detach() - detach buffers and release a dispatch
+ * @m2m_dev: mem2mem device
+ * @m2m_ctx: context of the running job
+ *
+ * Remove the current source and destination from their ready lists and finish
+ * the running job, without completing either buffer. The driver must save both
+ * buffer pointers before calling, retain ownership until hardware has stopped
+ * accessing them, and eventually complete them with v4l2_m2m_buf_done().
+ *
+ * This may be used by pipelined drivers on HOLD_CAPTURE-capable queues only
+ * for a source without V4L2_BUF_FLAG_M2M_HOLD_CAPTURE_BUF. Partial slices must
+ * instead use v4l2_m2m_buf_done_and_job_finish() to retain the capture buffer.
+ * The destination is no longer held or visible to subsequent m2m scheduling.
+ */
+void v4l2_m2m_job_finish_detach(struct v4l2_m2m_dev *m2m_dev,
+			      struct v4l2_m2m_ctx *m2m_ctx);
+
 /**
  * v4l2_m2m_buf_done_and_job_finish() - return source/destination buffers with
  * state and inform the framework that a job has been finished and have it
